## Screens & components annotated (all 11 screens)

**Shared components:** `Header` (all 7 authed/public pages), `ProductCard`, `FilterSidebar`, `SortDropdown`, `SearchBar`.

**Pages:** Index, ProductDetail, Categories, Cart, MyListings, CreateListing, Login, Register, About, NotFound.

## Id namespaces introduced

| Namespace | Covers |
|---|---|
| `nav.*` | Header — desktop links, cart badge, account menu, mobile drawer (`.mobile` suffixes) |
| `home.*` | Hero CTAs, 4 stats observables, `home.categories` collection |
| `products.*` | `products.grid` collection, count, empty state |
| `filters.*` | Sidebar + sort + search |
| `search.query` | Search input |
| `product.*` | Detail page — gallery, attributes, seller, add-to-cart, message dialog |
| `cart.*` | `cart.items` collection, total, checkout |
| `my-listings.*` | `my-listings.items` collection, `my-listings.delete-dialog.<id>` |
| `categories.*` | `categories.grid` collection |
| `listing.*` | Create-listing form |
| `login.*` / `register.*` / `about.*` / `not-found.*` | Auth + static pages |

## The one real hazard, and how it's handled

`FilterSidebar` renders its control set **twice internally** (desktop panel + mobile sheet) and Index mounts it **twice** — up to 4 DOM copies of the same controls. I threaded a **required** `scope` prop and parameterized the inner `FilterContent` with `idPrefix`, producing four disjoint namespaces: `filters.*`, `filters.sheet.*`, `filters.mobile.*`, `filters.mobile.sheet.*`. `ProductCard` likewise takes a required `collectionId`. Both are required rather than optional-with-default so TypeScript prevents a half-formed id from ever compiling.

## Collections that fold

`home.categories`, `products.grid`, `categories.grid`, `cart.items`, `my-listings.items`, and the four filter `categories`/`conditions` groups — each verified at runtime with ≥2 items under a genuine `role="collection"` DOM ancestor.

**Deliberately not folded:** the product-detail gallery thumbnails and create-listing photo slots. These are backed by array position with no stable domain key, so keying them would violate the spec's ban on index-keyed items. They use flat positional ids (`product.gallery.thumb-1`, `listing.photo-1.remove`) instead.

**Left unhinted:** decorative icons, layout wrappers, and `src/components/ui/*` shadcn primitives (hints live at the call sites that carry meaning).

## Verification

- **Skill validator:** 148 hinted elements, 74 files, **0 errors / 0 warnings**
- **Runtime DOM check** (the validator can't see ancestry or template-literal ids): I built SSR bundles and parsed the real output with `node-html-parser`, checking vocabulary, page-wide id uniqueness, collection ancestry, and ≥2-item folding. All 8 public routes clean — Index alone renders **136 hinted elements with 136 unique ids**, empirically confirming the four-copy filter namespacing. The 3 auth-gated screens returned `null` under SSR, so I ran a second pass in jsdom with a seeded session and cart: `/my-listings` 25/25 unique, `/cart` 22/22, `/create-listing` 20/20 — **AUTH ROUTES CLEAN**.
- **`tsc --noEmit`** exit 0 · **`npm run build`** succeeded
- **`npm run lint`**: 3 errors, all pre-existing in files I never touched (`ui/textarea.tsx`, `ui/command.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`). Zero problems in any edited file.

Two notes on process. First, my initial runtime checker used a hand-rolled regex tag-stack and reported 85 orphaned collection items; that was a bug in my scanner (treating a non-void tag as void pops the parent, so only the first sibling validates), not in the injection — I replaced it with a real HTML parser rather than "fixing" correct code. Second, all verification scaffolding is gone: the five harness files, three build dirs, the `dist/` output, and the `--no-save` dev packages are removed, and `package.json`/`package-lock.json` are untouched.

